    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0843" n="761" xml:id="pg761"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Commandant Givertoss to Mr. Chase</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 25, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The commander-in-chief of Tampico begs the consul of the United States to be
                    pleased to give him the names and Christian names of the individuals who have
                    this day entered this city, and who have not reported themselves at our office
                    He will be pleased to guarantee, under his responsibility, the good conduct of
                    these persons. In case he should not do so, the superior commandant will have
                    them arrested as vagabonds. We require an immediate reply.</p>
                <p>The superior commandant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>V DE GIVERTOSS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
